  "system": {
    "identifier": "hebi-basilisk-art-poison-cobra-dance",
    "description": "<p>You perform a string of graceful strikes each with the deadly precision of a cobra’s bite. Make two melee Taijutsu attacks, dealing your [Weapons Damage] + 1d8. If at least one attack scores a hit the affected creature must make a Strength saving throw being knocked Prone on a failure.</p>\n<p>Serpent Coil. If the last Bukijutsu cast benefitted from Chain 1, Chain 2 or Chain 3 then this jutsu increases the damage it deals by +1d8 for each chain rank beyond Chain 0 their last Bukijutsu was. (1d8, 2d8 or 3d8).</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For each rank you cast this jutsu above D-Rank, increase the cost of this jutsu by 3. If this jutsu is cast at B-Rank or higher, increase the number of attacks made by +1. If this jutsu is cast at S-Rank, increase the number of attacks made by +1.</p>",
